From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Taylor <zctaylor.work@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 17:19:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 16/30] Disable upstream TLS session resumption on the egress
 clusters

Envoy keeps one session cache per cluster and offers its newest session to
any SNI. An origin that accepts the ticket across SNI, as Cloudflare does,
answers with another host's certificate, and the SAN check fails with a
503.

Set max_session_keys to 0 on egress_forward_proxy and
egress_forward_proxy_grpc so every upstream connection does a full
handshake. A manifest test pins the setting. TestEgressUpstreamSessionPerSNI
runs the manifest clusters in Envoy against an origin that resumes across
SNI. It fails on the second host without the setting.

Fork-Topic: egress-tls-pools
Fork-Upstream: candidate
